From 29f25a6c20ed2aaf41e9a1590beef1c565ce1330 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Minkovsky <dminkovsky@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:52:27 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Show a search's rows as its window arrives and its count when
 it arrives
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A searching import list read its key at a position down one of two paths,
chosen by comparing a cost constant with the search's match count. The list
now reads one way at every size, and its count is a live query of its own.
The macOS list used to wait for the first window and the count before it
drew any row; it now draws the window when it arrives, stands the rows read
so far in for the count, and draws "… of …" in the filter field until the
count arrives.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
